(50622, 979, 656, '<td valign="top">Thanks to everyone who liked this.  It isn''t technically a black and white shot, as it went from colour to a final duotone shot, which gives the slight red tint to the ''blacks''  I liked this more than a pure B&amp;W, as I got married in a kilt with a lot of maroon, so it seemed appropriate.<br/><br/>I was suprised by the number of people that commented on the lack of anonymity - didn''t realise it would be such an issue.<br/></td>', 'Thanks to everyone who liked this.  It isn''t technically a black and white shot, as it went from colour to a final duotone shot, which gives the slight red tint to the ''blacks''  I liked this more than a pure B&W, as I got married in a kilt with a lot of maroon, so it seemed appropriate.I was suprised by the number of people that commented on the lack of anonymity - didn''t realise it would be such an issue.', '2002-04-29 08:38:00.000000', NULL, 0),
