(51714, 1054, 811, '<td valign="top">black and white suits this picture well.  would be a good shot for this week''s challenge as well.</td>', 'black and white suits this picture well.  would be a good shot for this week''s challenge as well.', '2002-04-27 13:04:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(51715, 1054, 888, '<td valign="top">My only concern with this is that it has been cut out but it could be because of a cloudy white sky.  Anyway, I really like the pic, it would work for the current "from the ground up" challenge too.</td>', 'My only concern with this is that it has been cut out but it could be because of a cloudy white sky.  Anyway, I really like the pic, it would work for the current "from the ground up" challenge too.', '2002-04-27 16:02:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(51716, 1054, 1070, '<td valign="top">shame you couldn''t resubmit this one next week.</td>', 'shame you couldn''t resubmit this one next week.', '2002-04-27 18:29:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(51717, 1054, 1031, '<td valign="top">I''d like this even better as an antry for the next challenge ("ground up").</td>', 'I''d like this even better as an antry for the next challenge ("ground up").', '2002-04-27 23:07:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(51718, 1054, 245, '<td valign="top">i wish I could read more of the text on the gravestone, nice hint of green</td>', 'i wish I could read more of the text on the gravestone, nice hint of green', '2002-04-28 19:28:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(51719, 1054, 27, '<td valign="top">It''s like you knew what the next challenge was going to be!!</td>', 'It''s like you knew what the next challenge was going to be!!', '2002-04-28 21:04:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(51720, 1054, 889, '<td valign="top">focus across the depth of field is very good. Still great detail on the top of the tombstone.</td>', 'focus across the depth of field is very good. Still great detail on the top of the tombstone.', '2002-04-28 23:11:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(51721, 1054, 933, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments all.  Very much enjoyed and appreciated.<br/><br/>Yes, yes, when I saw the ''Ground Up'' challenge after posting this pic, I thought "Crap!  I know what most of the comments are going to say!''<br/><br/>Some public responses to a few of the comments (not that anyone really gives a hoot)...<br/><br/>I did not think the grass would annoy people as much as it did. The intent there was, as Terrentius nailed it, to give the perpective of looking up at one''s own headstone.  The Grass also provided a way of obscuring some of the text, which I believed added an element of mystery (good call Gordon) and also helped to frame the date which, as reflected in the title, is the reference to the transition theme - the year this person passed away, transitioning into another state.   <br/><br/>Ahh well, maybe I thought about it too much...<br/><br/>As for the ''cutout'' sky, this picture was taken on a typically overcast and grey Washington day.  That caused the sky to be pretty washed out to begin with.  After desaturating, I adjusted the white point so that the sky was a clean white.<br/><br/><br/>Thanks again!<br/></td>', 'Thanks for the comments all.  Very much enjoyed and appreciated.Yes, yes, when I saw the ''Ground Up'' challenge after posting this pic, I thought "Crap!  I know what most of the comments are going to say!''Some public responses to a few of the comments (not that anyone really gives a hoot)...I did not think the grass would annoy people as much as it did. The intent there was, as Terrentius nailed it, to give the perpective of looking up at one''s own headstone.  The Grass also provided a way of obscuring some of the text, which I believed added an element of mystery (good call Gordon) and also helped to frame the date which, as reflected in the title, is the reference to the transition theme - the year this person passed away, transitioning into another state.   Ahh well, maybe I thought about it too much...As for the ''cutout'' sky, this picture was taken on a typically overcast and grey Washington day.  That caused the sky to be pretty washed out to begin with.  After desaturating, I adjusted the white point so that the sky was a clean white.Thanks again!', '2002-04-29 09:59:00.000000', NULL, 0),
